---
title: 'Editorial — Faye Wai'
description: 'Faye Wai — editorial strategy, research and synthesis, campaigns, and content operations. Journalism, technology, and independent research in the Canadian wine sector.'
ogTitle: 'Editorial — Faye Wai'
ogDescription: 'Editorial strategy, research, campaigns, and content operations.'
---
<main id="main">
<div class="wrap">

  <header class="hero hero--page grid grid--2" style="align-items:end">
    <div>
      <div class="eyebrow-rule" style="margin-bottom:clamp(26px,4vh,44px)"><span class="eyebrow">Editorial · Strategy · Research · Systems</span></div>
      <h1 class="display h1--page" style="font-size:clamp(38px,5.2vw,84px);max-width:14ch">I find the thread in messy things</h1>
      <div class="prose" style="margin-top:clamp(24px,3.4vh,38px);max-width:54ch">
        <p>In a past life — and occasionally in this one — I’ve worked across journalism, technology, editorial strategy, content operations, research, and brand campaigns.</p>
        <p>I’m happiest somewhere between a giant pile of information and the moment it finally makes sense: finding patterns, asking better questions, building structure, and turning complexity into something useful.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="btns" style="margin-top:clamp(28px,4vh,44px)">
        <a class="btn btn--solid" href="#work">Explore selected work ↓</a>
        <a class="btn" href="{{ site.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="board" data-reveal>
      <span class="board__label">On the desk</span>
      <ol class="board__list">
        {%- for s in editorial.services %}
        <li>{{ s.title }}</li>
        {%- endfor %}
      </ol>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section--rule" style="padding:clamp(50px,8vh,100px) 0" aria-labelledby="do-h">
    <div class="section-head section-head--stack" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow" id="do-h">01 / What I do</span>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:14px">Writer by trade. Operator by instinct.</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="tiles tiles--4" style="margin-top:clamp(26px,4vh,44px)">
      {%- for s in editorial.services %}
      <div class="svc" data-reveal>
        <span class="svc__num">0{{ loop.index }}</span>
        <h3 class="svc__title">{{ s.title }}</h3>
        <p class="svc__text">{{ s.text }}</p>
      </div>
      {%- endfor %}
    </div>
    <div style="margin-top:clamp(40px,6vh,64px)" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow eyebrow--faint" style="display:block">Brands I’ve worked with</span>
      <div class="cloud" style="margin-top:clamp(18px,2.6vh,26px)">
        {%- for b in editorial.brands %}
        <a href="{{ b.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="{{ b.name }}">
          {%- if b.logo %}<img src="assets/editorial/brands/{{ b.logo }}" alt="{{ b.name }}" loading="lazy">{% else %}<span>{{ b.name }}</span>{% endif %}
        </a>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--rule" style="padding:clamp(50px,8vh,100px) 0" aria-labelledby="career-h">
    <div class="section-head section-head--stack" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow" id="career-h">02 / A non-linear career, on purpose</span>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:14px">I’ve worn a few hats</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="track" data-reveal>
      {%- for t in editorial.timeline %}
      <li class="track__step">
        <span class="track__label">{{ t.step }}</span>
        <span class="track__role">{{ t.role }}</span>
        <span class="track__where">{{ t.where }}</span>
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ol>
    <p class="pull" data-reveal style="margin-top:clamp(36px,5vh,56px);max-width:34ch">Different industries, same instinct: understand the system, find what matters, and make it clearer.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section--rule grid grid--2" style="padding:clamp(50px,8vh,100px) 0" aria-labelledby="now-h">
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow" id="now-h">03 / Currently</span>
      <p class="pcard__meta" style="margin-top:16px">Recent consulting</p>
      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:14px;max-width:16ch">Turning industry complexity into something usable</h2>
    </div>
    <div data-reveal>
      <div class="prose" style="max-width:52ch">
        <p>Most recently I’ve been working within the Canadian wine sector on projects spanning interprovincial trade, export-market research, and comparative organisational analysis.</p>
        <p>The work involves moving between policy, market data, industry structures, stakeholder needs, and dozens of source trails — then synthesising it into practical frameworks, guides, and recommendations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="minis" style="margin-top:clamp(28px,4vh,40px)">
        {%- for c in editorial.consulting %}
        <div class="mini">
          <span class="mini__title">{{ c.title }}</span>
          <span class="mini__text">{{ c.text }}</span>
        </div>
        {%- endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {#- Bylines marked `featured` in _data/editorial.js. -#}
  <section id="work" class="section--rule" style="padding:clamp(50px,8vh,100px) 0 clamp(60px,9vh,110px)" aria-labelledby="bylines-h">
    <div class="section-head section-head--stack" data-reveal>
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow" id="bylines-h">04 / Selected bylines</span>
        <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:14px">Words in the wild</h2>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="blist">
      {%- for b in editorial.bylines %}{% if b.featured %}
      <a class="bl" href="{{ b.href }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
        <div class="bl__art frame r43{% if b.mark or not b.image %} frame--paper frame--mark{% endif %}">{% if b.image %}<img src="assets/editorial/work/{{ b.image }}" alt="{{ b.alt }}" loading="lazy">{% else %}<span class="frame__name">{{ b.pub }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
        <div class="bl__in">
          <span class="bl__pub">{{ b.pub }}</span>
          <h3 class="bl__title">{{ b.short or b.title }}</h3>
          <span class="bl__cta">{{ b.cta or 'Read' }} ↗</span>
        </div>
      </a>
      {%- endif %}{% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="padding:0 0 clamp(60px,9vh,110px)" aria-labelledby="thread-h">
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div data-reveal>
        <h2 class="h2" id="thread-h" style="max-width:12ch">Winding path, clear thread</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose" data-reveal style="max-width:52ch">
        <p>Journalism, technology, wine, research, operations, art and poetry can look like very different worlds.</p>
        <p>To me, they’ve always involved some version of the same practice: paying close attention, noticing patterns, asking questions, and finding a form for what I discover.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</div>

<section class="panel panel--rule">
  <div class="panel__in grid grid--2 grid--end">
    <div data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Work together</span>
      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:20ch">Research, editorial strategy, content operations</h2>
      <p class="prose prose--dark" style="margin-top:22px;max-width:48ch">Available for select freelance and advisory projects. Say hello with a line about what you’re making.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="btns" data-reveal>
      <a class="btn btn--solid" href="mailto:{{ site.email }}?subject=Editorial%20project" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Email Faye</a>
      <a class="btn" href="{{ site.linkedin }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn ↗</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</main>
